.idea/
node_modules/
# Fixture repositories ship tiny type stubs so the checker can resolve their
# imports without an install. The shared fixture node_modules stays ignored.
!fixtures/*/node_modules/
!fixtures/*/node_modules/**
!fixtures/*/*/node_modules/
!fixtures/*/*/node_modules/**
# A fixture holding two revisions of a project is one level deeper again.
!fixtures/*/*/*/node_modules/
!fixtures/*/*/*/node_modules/**
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
.flowatlas/
coverage/
*.log
.DS_Store

# Agent worktrees are checkouts of this repository, not content of it.
.claude/worktrees/
# Copies of fixture repositories that tests edit; removed when they finish.
fixtures/.scratch-*/
graph.html
# A project commits its own baseline; see docs/ci.md. This repository is the
# tool rather than a project being read, and the configuration here points at
# somebody's five repositories, so a baseline of them belongs to nobody.
flowatlas.baseline.json
# The marker two test processes use to agree who builds the fixture graph.
fixtures/multi-repo/.build-lock/

# Internal: the phase and defect tickets, the original plan, and a configuration
# that names somebody's own repositories. Kept beside the checkout rather than
# in it — none of it ever shipped in the package, and none of it belongs to
# anyone who clones this.
# Anchored to the root, every one of them. Unanchored, `flowatlas.config.json`
# matches at any depth and quietly swallowed all twelve fixture configurations,
# which the gate here could not see and the one on GitHub caught on its first
# run.
/roadmap/
# Both names: the tool was renamed and the file on disk was not, so the
# pattern stopped matching and one `git add -A` published 756 lines of
# internal planning to a public repository.
/flowatlas-plan.md
/flowmap-plan.md
/flowatlas.config.json

# Terminal recordings the demo driver keeps; the GIFs it renders are committed.
.demo-casts/

